Commands and subcommands (2.0)
- Register nested commands with inherited global/parent options and local args.
- Explicit dispatch invokes a command action after successful validation; parse
  remains action-free. Text and DocBook help follow the selected command path.
- All options follow the complete command path; misplaced options report a clear
  error. Applications without commands retain their existing behavior.

Unicode text and wide input
---------------------------

* UTF-8/UTF-16/UTF-32/wstring values and native Windows wchar_t argv support.
* Locale-independent Unicode.h conversion utilities reject malformed text.
* Unicode short flags, combined switches and UTF-8 constraint metadata.
* Help wrapping preserves UTF-8 scalar boundaries; raw string bytes remain intact.

Ordered value constraints
-------------------------

* Ready-made LessThanConstraint, LessThanOrEqualConstraint,
  GreaterThanConstraint and GreaterThanOrEqualConstraint own comparison bounds
  and generate usage/error text through the predicate core.
* Inclusive RangeConstraint remains available with unchanged boundary behavior.
* Ordered comparisons reject NaN values/bounds and avoid bound arithmetic.

Callable constraints
--------------------

* PredicateConstraint adapts owned functions and function objects; independent
  description and short ID strings supply error and usage text.
* MakeRuleConstraint shares rule state with computed descriptions and short IDs.
* C++20 MakeConstraint supports capturing lambdas, move-only callable
  state and const invocation. Empty callable objects fail at construction.

Argument aliases
----------------

* Arg::addAlias and labeled specs' aliases field add equivalent spellings.
* Unicode short aliases work in bundles; all aliases share argument state.
* Detailed text/DocBook help lists typed aliases; metadata snapshots own them.
